cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "JevCraft: a behavioural anti-cheat research bench for Minecraft (Paper)"
message: "If you use this bench or its findings, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "nft-syou"
    alias: nft-syou
license: MIT
version: 0.1.1
date-released: "2026-09-22"
keywords:
  - minecraft
  - anti-cheat
  - x-ray detection
  - behavioural telemetry
  - large language models
  - benchmark
abstract: >-
  JevCraft records mining-session telemetry from a Paper server, reduces it to a small typed
  feature object, asks a language model a few independent questions about it, and scores the
  result offline against labelled sessions. It exists to test one claim: whether behavioural
  telemetry catches X-Ray that ore-counting heuristics miss, at a matched false-positive rate.
  It never bans, kicks, or rolls back players; the strongest outcome is a request for human
  review.
